QUESTION : Demonstrate use of object- oriented programming concepts 

ALGORITHM:
1.Start
2.Define a class with attributes (course, campus)
3.Create object and access attributes
4.Define methods inside class and call using object
5.Take input using constructor (__init__)
6.Perform operations (like total marks)
7.Demonstrate inheritance:
8.Single inheritance (one parent → one child)
9.Multilevel inheritance (chain of classes)
10.Multiple inheritance (more than one parent)
11.Call methods using objects
12.Display output
13.Stop


CODE:
1. Class with Objects

class College:
    course1 = "BCA"
    course2 = "BCom"

c = College()

print("First course:", c.course1)
print("Second course:", c.course2)

2. Class with Method and Object

class College:
    course1 = "BCA"
    course2 = "BCom"
    campus1 = "Jayanagar"
    campus2 = "VV Puram"

    def university(self):
        print("Each course is in different campus")
        print(self.campus1, "offers", self.course1)
        print(self.campus2, "offers", self.course2)

c = College()
c.university()

3. Class with Input (Student Example)
class Student:
    def __init__(self):
        self.name = input("Enter student name: ")
        self.usn = input("Enter USN: ")
        self.m1 = int(input("Enter marks 1: "))
        self.m2 = int(input("Enter marks 2: "))
        self.m3 = int(input("Enter marks 3: "))

    def result(self):
        total = self.m1 + self.m2 + self.m3
        print("Student Result:", total)
        print("Name:", self.name)
        print("USN:", self.usn)

s = Student()
s.result()


4. Multiple Inheritance
class Teacher:
    def one(self):
        print("This is teacher of X grade")

class Student:
    def two(self):
        print("This is student of X grade")

class School(Teacher, Student):
    def three(self):
        print("Teacher and student belong to same school")

obj = School()
obj.one()
obj.two()
obj.three()

5. Multilevel Inheritance

class Father:
    def relation(self):
        name = input("Enter father name: ")
        print("Father:", name)

class Son(Father):
    def relation(self):
        age = int(input("Enter age: "))
        print("Son age:", age)

class Grandson(Son):
    def relation(self):
        asset = input("Enter asset: ")
        print("Asset:", asset)

f = Father()
f.relation()

s = Son()
s.relation()

g = Grandson()
g.relation()

6. Single Inheritance
class State:
    def geo(self):
        print("This is Karnataka")

class City(State):
    def geo(self):
        print("This is Bengaluru, Karnataka")

c = City()
c.geo()



